WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.540 --> 00:00:24.540
[ Music ]

00:00:27.240 --> 00:00:29.260
[Narrator:] Welcome to a dynamic video

00:00:29.262 --> 00:00:32.331
that will showcase the National 
Library of  Medicine's efforts

00:00:32.340 --> 00:00:36.320
to support seven awardees as
they use new technology

00:00:36.320 --> 00:00:40.300
to raise awareness and
disseminate HIV and AIDS information.

00:00:41.600 --> 00:00:45.040
[Porcha:] There is roughly a million
people living with HIV in the US

00:00:45.280 --> 00:00:47.440
and one in seven of them
don't even know it.

00:00:47.740 --> 00:00:50.400
This video reel will capture 
the innovative process

00:00:50.600 --> 00:00:53.380
each awardee took to spread
awareness about HIV

00:00:53.452 --> 00:00:55.455
through prevention and
treatment.

00:00:55.455 --> 00:00:58.457
We will show you how each
awardee organization

00:00:58.557 --> 00:01:01.461
created and executed their
NLM project

00:01:01.461 --> 00:01:04.797
and how it will be used to 
connect with their target group

00:01:04.797 --> 00:01:07.033
to increase HIV information.

00:01:07.040 --> 00:01:10.760
So let's start with awardees in
the Big Apple, New York City.

00:01:18.680 --> 00:01:25.760
[AIDS Patient:] He threw up his arms to the
ceiling, looked up and said,

00:01:25.760 --> 00:01:30.100
"There is no cure for AIDS
and there never will be."

00:01:30.920 --> 00:01:36.320
He said, "I can't take, handling
so many young people dying."

00:01:36.320 --> 00:01:38.460
He said, "I just cannot take it."

00:01:39.100 --> 00:01:43.260
[Narrator:] In 1994, at the height of the
AIDS epidemic, POZ Magazine,

00:01:43.260 --> 00:01:45.780
founded in New York City,
was first published.

00:01:45.880 --> 00:01:48.920
POZ stands for being
HIV positive.

00:01:49.540 --> 00:01:52.100
[Oriol:] It was also a time where there
was a lot of death

00:01:52.100 --> 00:01:53.380
and a lot of suffering.

00:01:53.680 --> 00:01:56.460
So it was a very bad environment
to be tested positive.

00:01:56.460 --> 00:02:00.420
[Narrator:] Oriol Gutierrez was diagnosed
with HIV in the nineties and

00:02:00.420 --> 00:02:03.680
has been a avid reader of the 
magazine since its inception.

00:02:03.780 --> 00:02:07.480
For years this magazine has been
a resource for him to learn how

00:02:07.480 --> 00:02:09.020
to survive with the virus.

00:02:09.280 --> 00:02:11.420
[Oriol:] I didn't think that I would see
the age of thirty.

00:02:11.860 --> 00:02:15.800
[Narrator:] He is forty-seven and now is the
Editor-in-Chief of POZ.

00:02:16.040 --> 00:02:20.060
The nationwide magazine reaches 
over 125,000 people

00:02:20.060 --> 00:02:23.820
with each issue, and has an
online version, POZ.com,

00:02:24.460 --> 00:02:27.540
which gets more than five 
million page views a month.

00:02:27.780 --> 00:02:31.620
POZ covers a wide spectrum of 
needs of people living with

00:02:31.620 --> 00:02:33.319
and effected by HIV and AIDS.

00:02:33.320 --> 00:02:36.500
[Oriol:] But when it comes to online,
there's also a portion of people

00:02:36.500 --> 00:02:39.060
that we still want to engage
with better.

00:02:40.080 --> 00:02:42.500
That's certainly people that are
more tech savvy.

00:02:42.780 --> 00:02:48.080
Younger people. People that are
at risk for HIV. Who are not

00:02:48.080 --> 00:02:50.980
necessarily living with the
virus, but need more information.

00:02:51.400 --> 00:02:54.640
[Narrator:] HIV and AIDS information from
the National Library of Medicine

00:02:55.000 --> 00:02:57.977
was a resource that brought
POZ and D'Vinci Interactive,

00:02:58.280 --> 00:03:01.920
a nationally recognized
educational and technology leader, together.

00:03:02.340 --> 00:03:06.540
D' Vinci Interactive saw POZ's
strong network and suggested

00:03:06.540 --> 00:03:10.580
interactive learning to
complement POZ online HIV news.

00:03:10.720 --> 00:03:14.020
[Mason:] Interactive learning takes a
topic that is usually text-based

00:03:14.020 --> 00:03:17.780
and puts it into a graphical 
multimedia format that grabs

00:03:17.780 --> 00:03:20.460
the user's attention and makes
them become involved and make

00:03:20.460 --> 00:03:23.080
key decisions really in the
learning process.

00:03:23.080 --> 00:03:26.260
[Narrator:] Mason Scuderi is Chief Operating
Officer for D'Vinci.

00:03:27.060 --> 00:03:31.240
With content from NLM and POZ,
his team was able to create

00:03:31.240 --> 00:03:34.060
interactive modules and
characters at the forefront

00:03:34.060 --> 00:03:35.140
of each story.

00:03:35.240 --> 00:03:37.880
[Mason:] So we start with the content
that's there. We pair that up

00:03:37.880 --> 00:03:41.660
with visual concepts early on
to see to make sure that both

00:03:41.660 --> 00:03:45.180
are consistent, and we bring
them together using interactive

00:03:45.560 --> 00:03:49.900
animation, sound, and just the
flow through the learning module

00:03:49.900 --> 00:03:52.480
itself and getting the user 
involved in making key

00:03:52.480 --> 00:03:53.360
decisions along the way.

00:03:53.720 --> 00:03:57.780
[Narrator:] The information from AIDSource
and AIDSinfo was vital in

00:03:57.780 --> 00:04:01.460
creating each module and its 
associated topic, like the

00:04:01.460 --> 00:04:04.980
aging module which Gutierrez
says has been especially helpful

00:04:04.980 --> 00:04:05.520
for him.

00:04:05.920 --> 00:04:08.680
[Oriol:] From the aging module I think
what I've taken away from it

00:04:08.680 --> 00:04:10.840
the best is the idea of self
empowerment.

00:04:11.220 --> 00:04:15.080
The idea of seeing people like 
myself who are living long term

00:04:15.080 --> 00:04:18.800
with the virus and how they've
gotten through the last several

00:04:18.800 --> 00:04:19.320
decades.

00:04:20.540 --> 00:04:22.360
Feeling that they can talk to
their doctor.

00:04:22.362 --> 00:04:25.064
Feeling that they have
information enough to make

00:04:25.164 --> 00:04:26.532
treatment decisions.

00:04:26.532 --> 00:04:29.869
[Narrator:] A partnership that connects 
information and technology

00:04:29.869 --> 00:04:33.005
together to help more people
hear and see

00:04:33.100 --> 00:04:34.940
how to live with HIV.

00:04:49.440 --> 00:04:51.960
[Narrator:] When you think of comic books
or graphic novels,

00:04:52.060 --> 00:04:56.240
what immediately comes to mind?
Batman? Superman?

00:04:56.500 --> 00:05:00.080
Well for digital illustrator 
Mike Lurry, he sees a tool

00:05:00.100 --> 00:05:01.860
to improve somebody's life.

00:05:02.360 --> 00:05:06.800
[Mile:] I am the illustrator for
this project and I also

00:05:06.900 --> 00:05:10.660
wrote the scripts for this
project, which is

00:05:10.700 --> 00:05:16.240
an HIV prevention campaign geared to the Latino community.

00:05:16.380 --> 00:05:18.940
[Narrator:] The campaign is called
Amigos y Amantes

00:05:18.951 --> 00:05:21.387
and it's being spearheaded
by El Centro,

00:05:21.387 --> 00:05:24.880
a non profit organization
that seeks to use interactive

00:05:24.880 --> 00:05:25.860
graphic novels.

00:05:26.060 --> 00:05:28.760
The novels raise awareness
raise awareness of HIV and AIDS

00:05:28.760 --> 00:05:31.340
for Latino MSM in
New York City.

00:05:31.600 --> 00:05:36.240
[Perez:] Latinos represent just 17% of
the population, but when it

00:05:36.540 --> 00:05:40.760
comes to the new cases of
HIV they represent almost

00:05:40.760 --> 00:05:43.760
25% of the cases
in the country.

00:05:44.140 --> 00:05:46.520
[Narrator:] The entire process starts
with focus groups

00:05:46.520 --> 00:05:48.100
held with community
members.

00:05:48.100 --> 00:05:51.280
[Anthony:] Initial focus groups were really
about message development.

00:05:51.700 --> 00:05:54.800
We said these are the key
HIV prevention messages.

00:05:55.240 --> 00:05:58.000
This is material that's posted
at the National Library of Medicine website.

00:05:58.180 --> 00:06:01.700
[Christel:] Here's a broad picture of what
we're thnking we're going to do.

00:06:01.700 --> 00:06:04.940
It's going to be an online
comic book, with voices

00:06:05.060 --> 00:06:07.280
and speech bubbles and
sometimes there might be

00:06:07.280 --> 00:06:09.520
choice points where the
action will stop

00:06:09.520 --> 00:06:11.840
and you'll decide for a
character whether they should

00:06:11.840 --> 00:06:13.260
or shouldn't 
do something.

00:06:13.300 --> 00:06:16.180
[Narrator:] Vital input from the community
members, coupled with the

00:06:16.180 --> 00:06:19.479
National Library of Medicine's 
resources, kickstart the

00:06:19.480 --> 00:06:22.100
scriptwriting and character
development process,

00:06:22.548 --> 00:06:25.440
with a focus on culturally
relatable content.

00:06:25.460 --> 00:06:30.200
[Perez:] They also need information
that is appropriate for them,

00:06:30.200 --> 00:06:31.940
that comes from their
experiences.

00:06:31.960 --> 00:06:35.540
Where the characters actually
look like them. Right?

00:06:35.700 --> 00:06:38.860
That they feel identified 
with those characters.

00:06:39.400 --> 00:06:43.820
[Narrator:] A task that was near and dear 
to the heart of illustrator, Mike Lurry.

00:06:44.120 --> 00:06:49.100
[Mike:] Having several Latino friends
and also living in a Latino community

00:06:49.360 --> 00:06:52.120
of Inwood in
Manhattan.

00:06:52.320 --> 00:06:53.760
It was very special to me.

00:06:54.080 --> 00:06:57.480
[Narrator:] Once the art was finished,
content development began.

00:06:57.550 --> 00:07:00.820
A key focus was to seemlessly
integrate NLM health education

00:07:00.880 --> 00:07:02.160
into the story.

00:07:02.300 --> 00:07:05.600
[Christel:] What we came up with is what we call
sort of a circle of friends structure.

00:07:05.640 --> 00:07:09.340
So there's one main character, 
and then these spokes that come

00:07:09.340 --> 00:07:09.960
out from him.

00:07:09.960 --> 00:07:12.760
So we know that he's
questioning. He's in the city.

00:07:12.760 --> 00:07:15.460
He's having sex with men
and with women, but he's also

00:07:15.460 --> 00:07:18.360
got a friend who's openly
out and he's got a cousin

00:07:18.600 --> 00:07:20.539
whose having problems
in her relationship.

00:07:20.700 --> 00:07:23.876
[Narrator:] Harnessing the power of
compelling stories to

00:07:23.876 --> 00:07:28.014
inspire readers to feel and
think deeply about health issues

00:07:28.020 --> 00:07:29.860
that directly affect them.

00:07:42.820 --> 00:07:46.580
Nestled between Philadelphia
and Pittsburgh sits the capital city

00:07:46.580 --> 00:07:48.580
of Pennsylvania. 
Harrisburg.

00:07:48.880 --> 00:07:51.340
Beyond having the unique
distinction as the training

00:07:51.360 --> 00:07:54.360
center for the Union Army
during the Civil War and the

00:07:54.380 --> 00:07:56.920
present location of the 
National Civil War Museum.

00:07:57.200 --> 00:08:00.260
Harrisburg now serves as
home to a new organization

00:08:00.480 --> 00:08:03.160
fighting a new battle:
Black Girl Health.

00:08:03.340 --> 00:08:05.960
[Porcha:] Black Girl Health is a
digital publishing company.

00:08:05.980 --> 00:08:09.380
Our mission is to transform
every day minority women

00:08:09.580 --> 00:08:11.420
into healthier individuals.

00:08:11.480 --> 00:08:16.380
We focus our efforts on social
media, online commercials, and community outreach.

00:08:16.740 --> 00:08:20.700
[Narrator:] In 2015 Black Girl Health
saw great success on Facebook,

00:08:20.920 --> 00:08:24.860
using articles and creating a
newscast to disseminate NLM

00:08:24.860 --> 00:08:28.000
information and resources as
part of the "Pop the Question"

00:08:28.000 --> 00:08:30.020
HIV Awareness campaign.

00:08:30.280 --> 00:08:32.920
[Ashley:] Pop the Question is really
just women taking control of

00:08:32.920 --> 00:08:33.880
their sexual health.

00:08:34.140 --> 00:08:36.200
When you think of Pop the
Question you probably think of

00:08:36.200 --> 00:08:38.517
a man getting down on one knee 
knee and asking their partner

00:08:38.520 --> 00:08:39.360
to marry them.

00:08:39.920 --> 00:08:43.160
Instead, this is the woman,
maybe not getting down on

00:08:43.180 --> 00:08:46.100
her knee, but asking that 
man to go get tested.

00:08:46.520 --> 00:08:50.000
[Narrator:] Using HIV information from
AIDSource and MedlinePlus,

00:08:50.120 --> 00:08:53.880
BGH expanded their "Pop the
Question" campaign in 2016

00:08:54.140 --> 00:08:57.136
to another social media
network frequently used by

00:08:57.136 --> 00:08:59.137
their target audience, 
Instagram.

00:08:59.140 --> 00:09:03.300
Social Media assistant Ashley
Manning converted text-based

00:09:03.300 --> 00:09:07.580
NLM articles to short format
videos, then published those

00:09:07.580 --> 00:09:10.480
videos weekly on the BGH
Instagram page

00:09:10.480 --> 00:09:11.620
for it's followers.

00:09:12.120 --> 00:09:15.287
[Ashley:] HIV is definitely a sensitive
topic. It's something that a lot

00:09:15.287 --> 00:09:17.322
of people don't feel comfortable
talking about.

00:09:17.322 --> 00:09:21.200
There's definitely a huge stigma
around HIV in the minority community.

00:09:21.520 --> 00:09:25.240
So bringing this information
to them on social media through video,

00:09:25.540 --> 00:09:27.820
it makes them feel 
more comfortable sharing it

00:09:27.820 --> 00:09:29.400
and talking about it 
with others.

00:09:29.400 --> 00:09:31.480
[Narrator:] To help in the fight to
raise awareness,

00:09:31.560 --> 00:09:35.220
BGH recruited help 
from social media influencer,

00:09:35.260 --> 00:09:35.960
Miss Jay DMV.

00:09:35.960 --> 00:09:37.580
[Miss Jay DMV:] So how many women 
has he been with?

00:09:37.580 --> 00:09:39.420
Oh. Heather, Marie and 
Tonya.

00:09:39.680 --> 00:09:41.200
That's not bad. Three.

00:09:41.280 --> 00:09:45.620
And Brittany. And Tonya's
sister. And Mackenzie...

00:09:45.680 --> 00:09:48.060
Ladies are you unsure
about your man's HIV status?

00:09:48.160 --> 00:09:50.120
If so, it might be time to
pop the question.

00:09:50.300 --> 00:09:51.960
Visit BlackGirlHealth.com today

00:09:51.960 --> 00:09:53.180
and we'll show you how.

00:09:53.400 --> 00:09:56.360
Bringing comedy to a topic
that isn't fun to talk about

00:09:56.360 --> 00:09:58.940
really made the content
more engaging.

00:09:58.940 --> 00:10:01.460
[Narrator:] Capitalizing on the viral
reach of the video

00:10:01.460 --> 00:10:04.360
Miss Jay instructed her
following to navigate to

00:10:04.360 --> 00:10:07.773
the BGH website where they
could fill out a survey

00:10:07.773 --> 00:10:10.743
evaluating their knowledge
of HIV and how to

00:10:10.743 --> 00:10:11.860
pop the question.

00:10:12.000 --> 00:10:15.715
[Karlise:] It opened up a avenue
for us to have a dialogue

00:10:15.720 --> 00:10:18.920
about how to pop the question,
when to pop the question,

00:10:18.940 --> 00:10:21.320
if you have popped
the question correctly.

00:10:21.720 --> 00:10:25.520
[Narrator:] BGH Staff Assistant Karlise
Cureton played an integral role

00:10:25.520 --> 00:10:28.620
in turning our digital 
interactions with minority women

00:10:28.740 --> 00:10:31.840
into real world actions at 
Black Girl Health's second

00:10:31.840 --> 00:10:34.580
annual Kickstart health and
wellness expo.

00:10:34.800 --> 00:10:38.440
[Karlise:] As a part of our Pop the Question
campaign, we are here at the

00:10:38.440 --> 00:10:41.740
Kickstart women's health expo 
and we are offering women

00:10:41.740 --> 00:10:43.780
an option to get screened
for HIV.

00:10:43.900 --> 00:10:47.740
[Narrator:] The increased awareness of NLM's
HIV information on social media

00:10:48.200 --> 00:10:50.880
encouraged women to not 
only attend the expo,

00:10:51.300 --> 00:10:54.260
but garnered several 
on site testings as well.

00:10:54.540 --> 00:10:58.140
Showing once and for all
in the battle for minority

00:10:58.140 --> 00:11:01.780
women's health in Harrisburg, 
allies prove more powerful

00:11:01.780 --> 00:11:03.340
than obstacles.

00:11:22.180 --> 00:11:26.880
HIV is a tide. The tidewater
region has not been able to turn.

00:11:27.240 --> 00:11:30.580
Norfolk State University
is helping lead the community

00:11:30.660 --> 00:11:33.300
out of the rocky waters
with Project Choice.

00:11:33.900 --> 00:11:38.097
[Desi:] Project Choice is an HIV
education and prevention program

00:11:38.097 --> 00:11:41.500
so the choice stands for choosig
healthy options in challenging

00:11:41.500 --> 00:11:42.580
environments.

00:11:42.580 --> 00:11:45.260
[Narrator:] The university program has
focused on meeting the health

00:11:45.260 --> 00:11:49.460
needs of African-Americans by
using technology to access information.

00:11:49.720 --> 00:11:53.100
[Tiphanie:] I think the mission of this
project is really in line with

00:11:53.100 --> 00:11:54.360
the overall mission of 
Project Choice,

00:11:54.360 --> 00:11:58.540
which is to not only educate
students and community members

00:11:58.540 --> 00:12:02.000
that we engage with, but to try
to prevent the spread of HIV.

00:12:02.140 --> 00:12:05.440
[Narrator:] To disseminate information from
the National Library of Medicine,

00:12:05.600 --> 00:12:08.494
engineer student Keturah
Caldwell created an iBook.

00:12:08.740 --> 00:12:10.840
[Keturah:] We were able to put the
iBook together through

00:12:10.840 --> 00:12:13.480
of course the software
iBooks Author.

00:12:13.800 --> 00:12:16.780
[Narrator:] Caldwell says multiple widgets
are in the software,

00:12:16.900 --> 00:12:20.500
which provide the ability to include
interactive media, such as

00:12:20.500 --> 00:12:22.680
audio and video that the
reader can play.

00:12:23.020 --> 00:12:26.400
Some of which are recorded
skits from theater students at Norfolk State

00:12:26.400 --> 00:12:28.580
[Student 1:] You're not afraid or timid
when you speak.

00:12:30.220 --> 00:12:33.020
[Student 2:] But...what would we say to 
our partners exactly, like...?

00:12:33.760 --> 00:12:36.560
With my intuition I 
can't help but feel as though

00:12:37.160 --> 00:12:41.700
all men are up to no good
and are never trying to actually listen

00:12:41.700 --> 00:12:43.380
to what you're doing and
what your're saying.

00:12:43.520 --> 00:12:49.740
[Precious:] So I took the role as being
this ideal aggressive woman

00:12:49.740 --> 00:12:54.200
who had been sexually harassed,
violated, you name it.

00:12:54.240 --> 00:12:57.760
Protect yourself. 
Don't neglect yourself.

00:12:57.760 --> 00:13:01.240
[Narrator:] AIDSinfo and MedlinePlus were
the resources used to bring

00:13:01.240 --> 00:13:02.780
context to the scripts.

00:13:02.780 --> 00:13:06.560
[Precious:] She became informed with the
PREP the information of HIV,

00:13:06.900 --> 00:13:10.760
how to go get help, and who to
talk to, where to go,

00:13:10.760 --> 00:13:15.060
so on and so forth, and 
her character changed.

00:13:15.060 --> 00:13:18.000
[Keturah:] So embedded in the iBook are
questions that they ask

00:13:18.000 --> 00:13:19.640
and then it gives you the 
right answer to tell you

00:13:19.740 --> 00:13:20.880
whether you're right or
wrong.

00:13:21.000 --> 00:13:23.980
So that's embedded in several
of the chapters to make sure

00:13:23.980 --> 00:13:26.000
that people are understanding 
what they're reading.

00:13:26.000 --> 00:13:28.440
[ Greek Life Crowd Clapping ]

00:13:28.440 --> 00:13:32.600
[Narrator:] Project Choice realizes the real
test is outside the boundaries

00:13:32.600 --> 00:13:35.300
of campus life and in the
community.

00:13:35.460 --> 00:13:38.751
Cynthia Burwell is tasked with 
taking the iBook

00:13:38.751 --> 00:13:39.418
to the churches.

00:13:39.651 --> 00:13:41.220
[Cynthia:] The church helps to reach the
people.

00:13:41.260 --> 00:13:47.340
They will be trained on how to
use the iBook for AIDS and HIV

00:13:47.680 --> 00:13:49.180
education in their churches.

00:13:49.420 --> 00:13:52.020
They will be able to use it 
with different groups in their

00:13:52.020 --> 00:13:56.100
churches to provide up to
date information.

00:13:57.680 --> 00:14:01.220
[Narrator:] NLM information that's helping
give a innovative lifeline

00:14:01.220 --> 00:14:03.920
to protect the 
Tidewater community.

00:14:25.340 --> 00:14:28.860
[Porcha:] You have just seen how innovatie
projects on the East Coast

00:14:28.860 --> 00:14:33.360
are fighting the HIV epidemic 
with NLM educational tools.

00:14:33.560 --> 00:14:36.840
Community outreach 
organizations, colleges,

00:14:36.842 --> 00:14:38.810
tech and digital companies,

00:14:38.944 --> 00:14:42.981
print and online publications
are all playing an integral role

00:14:42.981 --> 00:14:44.460
in making a difference.

00:14:44.620 --> 00:14:48.140
So now we're going to visit 
organization and communities

00:14:48.140 --> 00:14:52.300
further west. Starting in the
Windy City: Chicago, Illinois.

00:14:52.560 --> 00:14:55.720
Where there's an increase of 
HIV AIDS related cases

00:14:56.040 --> 00:14:58.040
among African-American
men.

00:15:01.560 --> 00:15:05.136
At the close of 2015,
more than 24,000 people

00:15:05.140 --> 00:15:07.620
were living with HIV in
Chicago, Illinois.

00:15:08.020 --> 00:15:10.840
Proactive, a local nonprofit
organization,

00:15:11.060 --> 00:15:14.840
is on the front lines, training
and equipping community health

00:15:14.980 --> 00:15:17.715
workers on how to deal with 
the HIV epidemic.

00:15:17.740 --> 00:15:20.760
[Eula:] There are actually four 
institutions involved,

00:15:20.760 --> 00:15:22.760
two community based
institutions,

00:15:22.760 --> 00:15:24.360
and two academic
institutions.

00:15:24.780 --> 00:15:29.680
One is South Suburban 
College and that's out here

00:15:29.820 --> 00:15:31.880
and that's a two year
instituiton.

00:15:31.880 --> 00:15:35.500
And the other is Chicago 
State University.

00:15:35.500 --> 00:15:38.100
[Narrator:] These Step Up students 
will eventually become

00:15:38.140 --> 00:15:41.160
community health workers, 
helping residents by

00:15:41.160 --> 00:15:44.200
educating them on HIV
prevention and treatment methods

00:15:44.400 --> 00:15:46.040
through the use of tablets.

00:15:46.180 --> 00:15:48.513
[Felisha:] I know that in the future, with
the career choice

00:15:48.520 --> 00:15:51.060
that I've chosen, this is going
to be a great tool for me

00:15:51.060 --> 00:15:55.580
because information that I share
will be from a reliable source.

00:15:55.580 --> 00:15:59.880
[Narrator:] Proactive will train 93 Step Up
students on NLM resources.

00:16:00.120 --> 00:16:02.694
This will be part of an
interactive digital lesson plan

00:16:02.700 --> 00:16:05.240
and Proactive's healthcare readiness program.

00:16:05.580 --> 00:16:10.300
[Ethel:] I thought that I had the
resources that I needed to talk about HIV

00:16:10.560 --> 00:16:13.140
but as I began to go on 
this particular website,

00:16:13.740 --> 00:16:17.140
I learned more and more
and it was more truthful

00:16:17.141 --> 00:16:18.410
and accurate information.

00:16:18.480 --> 00:16:21.160
[Narrator:] The tablets community health
workers learn to navigate

00:16:21.160 --> 00:16:25.940
NLM resources on will prove
useful at off site partner organizations.

00:16:26.260 --> 00:16:29.260
Allowing them the opportunity 
to meet people where they are

00:16:29.500 --> 00:16:33.460
with vital and accurate HIV 
prevention and treatment information

00:16:33.520 --> 00:16:38.860
[Eula:] We have high risk populations,
so they are hard to find, hard to locate.

00:16:39.060 --> 00:16:42.620
But our team has really
been able to go in there

00:16:42.620 --> 00:16:47.800
and do segmented outreach
and locate those individuals

00:16:47.800 --> 00:16:48.980
that are positive.

00:16:49.180 --> 00:16:52.440
[Narrator:] Increasing numbers of 
qualified health care workers

00:16:52.440 --> 00:16:56.180
to meet the increasing need
to treat HIV patients.

00:17:06.260 --> 00:17:08.800
On any given day, one to
two hundred people

00:17:08.800 --> 00:17:10.660
pass through the Mexican
Consulate

00:17:10.760 --> 00:17:12.320
in Salt Lake City, Utah.

00:17:12.460 --> 00:17:15.440
And a good portion of those 
people are just waiting.

00:17:16.040 --> 00:17:19.371
[Alejandra:] And there's absolutely nothing 
there to do, they just sit there

00:17:19.371 --> 00:17:21.173
and stare at the wall pretty much.

00:17:21.180 --> 00:17:23.600
So we use that time 
with a "promotora,"

00:17:23.600 --> 00:17:24.780
or community health worker.

00:17:25.080 --> 00:17:27.012
[Narrator:] And they take full advantage 
of it.

00:17:27.120 --> 00:17:29.714
Transforming waiting time 
into a meaningful

00:17:29.714 --> 00:17:31.482
health learning experience.

00:17:31.482 --> 00:17:34.580
[Alejandra:] The biggest way that HIV has
effected our community members

00:17:34.580 --> 00:17:37.620
is the fact that it's not
something that we talk about

00:17:38.060 --> 00:17:41.460
and it's not something that
we necessarily know about.

00:17:41.780 --> 00:17:44.620
[Narrator:] Getting pertinent health
information from a familiar face

00:17:45.040 --> 00:17:47.632
also makes a big impact on
those served.

00:17:47.640 --> 00:17:48.140
[speaking in Spanish]

00:18:09.440 --> 00:18:11.660
[Narrator:] Information they may have never
come across

00:18:11.780 --> 00:18:14.659
due to the language barriers 
they face in the US

00:18:14.659 --> 00:18:16.862
and the cultural barriers 
they face back home.

00:18:16.862 --> 00:18:19.498
[Alejandra:] We invite them into the
Ventanilla de Salud

00:18:19.498 --> 00:18:20.766
to get tested.

00:18:20.766 --> 00:18:25.100
We do blood pressure, glucose 
and BMI testing and at the end

00:18:25.100 --> 00:18:28.140
of every person coming in 
to getting the testing

00:18:28.140 --> 00:18:31.360
we do a one-on-one session
to go over the websites again,

00:18:31.360 --> 00:18:34.120
to reinforce that these websites
are available to them

00:18:34.120 --> 00:18:37.916
to get HIV AIDS info but also
other health related information.

00:18:37.920 --> 00:18:39.460
[Speaker:] Ciriac Alvares

00:18:39.860 --> 00:18:42.780
[Narrator:] They've connected over 300
people to health resources

00:18:42.788 --> 00:18:44.956
with the help of the
National Library of Medicine,

00:18:45.080 --> 00:18:46.680
including Ciriac Alvarez.

00:18:46.980 --> 00:18:48.580
There is one website in 
particular

00:18:48.580 --> 00:18:51.220
that Alejandra showed me 
where you can find

00:18:51.220 --> 00:18:54.560
like HIV testing places by like
putting in your zip code

00:18:54.560 --> 00:18:55.960
and it's really cool.

00:18:55.967 --> 00:18:59.805
[Alejandra:] From those surveys we've been
able to realize that

00:18:59.905 --> 00:19:03.541
the work that our "promotoras"
are doing is valuable and it

00:19:03.541 --> 00:19:07.040
works because we see an increase
of knowledge from the before

00:19:07.040 --> 00:19:09.920
and after of our community
members when they receive the

00:19:09.920 --> 00:19:12.180
workshop and are able to
access their resources.

00:19:12.320 --> 00:19:15.253
[Narrator:] Assisting yet another person
to their right to

00:19:15.260 --> 00:19:18.940
life, liberty, and the pursuit
of healthiness.

00:19:36.560 --> 00:19:39.240
Time Magazine dubbed
the year 2014

00:19:39.240 --> 00:19:41.279
the Transgender Tipping
Point.

00:19:41.480 --> 00:19:43.340
From the red carpet and
the runway,

00:19:43.880 --> 00:19:47.151
to politics and entertainment, 
transgender people

00:19:47.151 --> 00:19:48.853
truly were everywhere.

00:19:48.860 --> 00:19:50.820
But for many transgender
youth,

00:19:50.920 --> 00:19:54.520
the notoriety has not created
impactful change in their

00:19:54.520 --> 00:19:55.520
daily lives.

00:19:55.820 --> 00:19:57.195
Nowhere is that more
apparent

00:19:57.580 --> 00:19:59.140
than in the area of
healthcare.

00:19:59.360 --> 00:20:02.860
[Bhubendra:] Transgender youth they have
challenges

00:20:02.867 --> 00:20:04.703
they have requirements

00:20:04.703 --> 00:20:06.700
and they don't know where
to go to get

00:20:06.700 --> 00:20:07.500
their questions answered.

00:20:07.539 --> 00:20:09.274
They don't know where to go
to get services

00:20:09.280 --> 00:20:10.580
that are youth friendly,

00:20:10.780 --> 00:20:14.040
with providers that understand 
the needs that are quite unique

00:20:14.045 --> 00:20:15.213
for the Transgender community.

00:20:15.220 --> 00:20:17.380
[Narrator:] Headquartered in the Bay Area
of California.

00:20:17.860 --> 00:20:19.980
The mecca of LGBTQ rights.

00:20:19.984 --> 00:20:24.188
YTH is the partner of choice 
for those in search of new ways

00:20:24.188 --> 00:20:26.992
to advance health of youth
and young adults

00:20:26.992 --> 00:20:27.992
through technology.

00:20:27.992 --> 00:20:29.861
[James:] In addition to those health
disparities

00:20:29.861 --> 00:20:32.564
youth are also kind of
faced with, they're dependent

00:20:32.564 --> 00:20:33.331
on their parents.

00:20:33.465 --> 00:20:35.066
They don't necessarily have
an income.

00:20:35.066 --> 00:20:36.901
So if they come out to their
parents

00:20:36.901 --> 00:20:38.620
and they're not receiving 
support,

00:20:39.040 --> 00:20:40.400
I mean where do you go 
from there?

00:20:40.400 --> 00:20:43.074
[Narrator:] And that is why they
developed they2ze.

00:20:43.080 --> 00:20:46.140
A mobile app that brings 
together all the Bay Area

00:20:46.140 --> 00:20:48.640
resources for transgender
spectrum youth.

00:20:48.920 --> 00:20:52.880
[Julie:] So the design itself was really
guided by our brainstorming

00:20:52.880 --> 00:20:56.754
process and meeting with the
transgender youth community

00:20:56.760 --> 00:20:58.160
and our advisory board.

00:20:58.220 --> 00:21:00.591
So that sort of kicked off the
design process where we got

00:21:00.600 --> 00:21:03.880
feedback from them on what they 
would like to see in the app.

00:21:04.020 --> 00:21:06.120
[Bhubendra:] When somebody uses the app and 
they are searching

00:21:06.120 --> 00:21:10.600
for a certain answer,
a certain search term

00:21:10.920 --> 00:21:13.520
a lot of the resources that end
up coming up

00:21:13.520 --> 00:21:14.900
are actually NLM resources.

00:21:14.900 --> 00:21:18.420
[Narraotr:] The app is available in the 
Apple or Android app store

00:21:18.420 --> 00:21:21.079
and has features that allow 
you to find community hangouts,

00:21:21.500 --> 00:21:25.000
testing sites, and doctors
like Doctor Scott Mosser

00:21:25.000 --> 00:21:28.720
an internationally renowned
board-certifed plastic surgeon

00:21:28.720 --> 00:21:30.080
based in San Francisco.

00:21:30.180 --> 00:21:34.400
[Dr. Mosser:] I think the app is expansive
for trans healthcare resources.

00:21:34.400 --> 00:21:38.100
So any individual that's 
looking for an HIV doctor,

00:21:38.200 --> 00:21:41.240
[?] blood pressure doctor,
or a diabetes doctor

00:21:41.680 --> 00:21:44.100
for any reason but wants to
make sure that they're

00:21:44.100 --> 00:21:48.420
gender inclusive and
understanding of their

00:21:48.420 --> 00:21:49.640
potential gender needs
as well.

00:21:50.260 --> 00:21:52.340
Those are the individuals all
who would be using the app.

00:21:52.340 --> 00:21:54.700
[Narrator:] Giving Bay Area transgender 
youth

00:21:54.712 --> 00:21:56.948
their moment for a
better life.

00:22:09.800 --> 00:22:12.260
[Porcha:] You have just seen the 
technical processes

00:22:12.260 --> 00:22:17.320
each ACIOP awardee took to 
disseminate NLM HIV information.

00:22:17.460 --> 00:22:20.140
D'Vinci upgraded a conventional 
print magazine

00:22:20.140 --> 00:22:22.140
with a scenario based e-learning
module

00:22:22.140 --> 00:22:24.540
interwoven with resources 
from NLM.

00:22:24.940 --> 00:22:27.779
El Centro used interactive
graphic novels

00:22:28.100 --> 00:22:30.500
to disseminate NLM information.

00:22:30.860 --> 00:22:34.100
Black Girl Health used an 
influential social media

00:22:34.100 --> 00:22:36.180
celebrity to bring minority
women together

00:22:36.280 --> 00:22:38.740
to learn about NLM 
information resources.

00:22:39.460 --> 00:22:42.540
Norfolk State University
developed iBooks

00:22:42.540 --> 00:22:45.860
that combined dramatic
arts with NLM information

00:22:45.860 --> 00:22:47.320
to engage youth.

00:22:47.760 --> 00:22:50.860
Proactive Community Services
engaged students

00:22:50.868 --> 00:22:52.370
pursuing health careers

00:22:52.370 --> 00:22:54.372
to use tablets to become
proficient

00:22:54.380 --> 00:22:55.940
with NLM resources.

00:22:56.400 --> 00:22:59.277
Communities United used
the Mexican Consulate

00:22:59.277 --> 00:23:01.012
as a technology center 
to educate

00:23:01.012 --> 00:23:04.216
Spanish speaking immigrants
on NLM resources

00:23:04.220 --> 00:23:05.780
and HIV information.

00:23:06.280 --> 00:23:09.880
And lastly, YTH served 
transgender youth

00:23:09.888 --> 00:23:12.557
by developing a mobile 
phone app

00:23:12.560 --> 00:23:15.693
using NLM information 
to meet the special needs

00:23:15.900 --> 00:23:17.560
of this population

00:23:17.780 --> 00:23:19.831
After showing all the
technical approaches

00:23:19.831 --> 00:23:22.367
used to disseminate
NLM resources

00:23:22.367 --> 00:23:24.135
we hope you see the 
awardees

00:23:24.140 --> 00:23:26.920
as key stakeholders 
that aligned their efforts

00:23:26.920 --> 00:23:29.200
to address an ongoing 
health crisis.

00:23:29.500 --> 00:23:31.676
In addition, the National 
Library of Medicine

00:23:31.860 --> 00:23:34.812
as an emerging leader in
innovative approaches

00:23:34.820 --> 00:23:37.315
to raising awareness
around HIV and AIDS.

00:23:37.560 --> 00:23:39.651
We'd like to thank NLM
for promoting

00:23:39.651 --> 00:23:41.853
cutting edge technology 
to support

00:23:41.860 --> 00:23:44.860
HIV and AIDS prevention 
and treatment information.

00:23:45.160 --> 00:23:47.258
As well as supporting each
awardees

00:23:47.260 --> 00:23:50.320
creative uses of
NLM's resources.

00:23:50.320 --> 00:24:09.560
[ Music ]

